LOCAL1="Sound defaults of this computer"
LOCAL2="Rates the sound system may switch to, so a file plays at its own rate: %s Hz"
LOCAL3="Rate when nothing plays: %s Hz"
LOCAL4="Every computer gets 44100 Hz (the audio CD) and 48000 Hz (the professional standard, AES5). The rest comes from the sound devices found here:"
LOCAL5="  %s: %s Hz, %s"
LOCAL6="up to %s bit"
LOCAL7="16 bit only"
LOCAL8="  %s: its rates could not be read, so the standard rates are kept for it and PipeWire decides what the device takes."
LOCAL9="A file whose rate the device cannot play is converted once, to the nearest rate the device takes."
LOCAL10="Conversion quality: %s of 14, the highest this processor carries (the heaviest conversion, 192000 to 48000 Hz, takes %s %% of one core; the limit is %s %%)."
LOCAL11="Sample format: each device is opened in the best format it offers, 24 bit or more where it has it."
LOCAL12="A device that takes only 16 bit gets triangular dither, so quiet passages and fades stay clean. To switch it off, see the comment in the file named below."
LOCAL13="Your own settings win: put them in ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d or ~/.config/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d, or in /etc with a file name that sorts after 00-sparky-stereo-audio."
LOCAL14="These choices were made for %s and are written in %s."
LOCAL15="No sound device was found, so only the standard rates are set."
LOCAL16="No choices are recorded yet. Run: sudo sparky-stereo-audio detect --write"
LOCAL17="Conversion quality: %s of 14 (this processor was not measured, so PipeWire's own quality stays)."
LOCAL18="The sound defaults have not been written yet, so there is nothing to apply. Run: sudo sparky-stereo-audio detect --write"
LOCAL19="The sound system of this session did not answer, so the rates it follows were not updated. Start it and run: sparky-stereo-audio apply"
LOCAL20="The sound devices %s could not be read, so the standard rates are kept for them and PipeWire decides what each device takes. Repair: sudo sparky-stereo-audio detect --write"
LOCAL21="The sound settings could not be written to %s (%s), so nothing was changed there. Check that the disk is writable and has free space, then: sudo sparky-stereo-audio detect --write"
LOCAL22="%s is not the file this package wrote, so it was left as it is, because your own file wins. The package's choice for it is not in use. Remove or rename your file to get the package's choice."
LOCAL23="The conversion quality of this processor could not be measured (%s), so PipeWire's own quality 4 stays. Repair: sudo sparky-stereo-audio detect --write"
